Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force three months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to decision on elected president of board of directors)
The amended provisions of Article 27-4 shall begin to apply to the public official first dispatched after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to entrustment of election management by Chairperson of National Federation)
The amended provisions of Article 72-9 shall begin to apply to the Chairperson of the National Federation first elected after this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Special cases concerning term of office and election following simultaneous election of presidents of local unions)
(1) Notwithstanding Article 31(1), where the term of office of the president has begun or is to begin during the period from the enforcement date of this Act to November 21, 2023, the term of office of the president shall be until November 20, 2025.
(2) Where the term of office of a president who is newly elected or whose term of office begins since November 22, 2019 before this Act enters into force expires and another term of office begins accordingly, the term of office of the relevant president shall be until November 20, 2029, notwithstanding Article 31(1).
(3) The election of the president of a union following his or her predecessor whose term of office expires pursuant to paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be held for the first time simultaneously pursuant to the following subparagraphs, and the election of a succeeding president following the expiration of his or her term of office shall be held on a second Wednesday of November of the relevant year when the expiration date falls:
1. The simultaneous election day of a succeeding president of his or her predecessor whose term of office expires pursuant to paragraph (1): Nov. 12, 2025.
2. The simultaneous election day of a succeeding president of his or her predecessor whose term of office expires pursuant to paragraph (2): Nov. 14, 2029.
(4) The term of office of the president elected through re-election or by-election after November 22, 2023 shall be the remaining term of office of his or her predecessor; provided, where the period from the date on which the reason for holding such election arises to the expiration date of the term of office is less than 1 year, no re-election or by-election shall be held.
(5) The term of office of the president elected by a union falling under any of the following subparagraphs after Nov. 22, 2023 shall be until the expiration date of the relevant simultaneous election term, if the period from the commencement date of his or her term of office to the expiration date of the term under paragraph (1) (including the expiration date of the term of office every four years afterwards; hereinafter referred to as "simultaneous election date upon term expiration") shall be at least two years, and if the period from the commencement date of his or her term of office to the first simultaneous election upon term expiration is less than two years, the term of office shall be until the next simultaneous election date upon term expiration:
1. A union newly established pursuant to Article 7;
2. A union merged or divided pursuant to Article 55;
(6) In any of the following cases, the relevant union need not hold a simultaneous election of a president under paragraph (3) in accordance with a resolution of the board of directors:
1. When a resolution is adopted on a merger pursuant to Article 55(1) of the Act:
2. When the Financial Services Commission or the Chairperson of the National Federation recommends not to hold an election for any of the following reasons:
a. Where a merger is recommended, requested, or ordered under this Act;
b. Where it is impracticable to hold an election due to a financial accident of a large amount, natural disaster, etc.
(7) Where the simultaneous election of a president has not been held pursuant to paragraph (6) but a union no longer falls under any subparagraph of paragraph (6), the election day of a president shall be designated without delay by a resolution of the board of directors and the election shall be held within 30 days. In such cases, the term of office of the president shall be the remainder of the term of office of a president who fails to be elected because the simultaneous election of the president under paragraph (3) has not been held, and where the period is less than one year, the relevant election of the president shall not be held.
(8) Where the term of office of the president is reduced pursuant to paragraph (1), (2) or (5), the relevant term of office shall not be included in the number of times the consecutive appointment is restricted under the proviso to Article 31(1).
(9) Where a president is not elected pursuant to the proviso to paragraph (4) or the latter part of paragraph (7), the duties of the president shall be performed by an acting director under Article 27(5) in accordance with the following subparagraphs:
1. Where no re-election or special election is held pursuant to the proviso to paragraph (4): Until the expiration date of the term of office of the predecessor;
2. Where a president is not elected pursuant to the latter part of paragraph (7): Until the expiration date of the term of office of a president who fails to be elected because the simultaneous election of a president under paragraph (3) is not held.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning entrustment of president election to Gu/Si/Gun election commission)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 27-3, a president election to be held after the enforcement of this Act before the simultaneous election date under each subparagraph of Article 4(3) of Addenda shall be governed by the previous provisions.

